cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mlmr, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "mlmr: A Guided Interface for Mixed-Effects and Multilevel Models"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-02"
authors:
  - family-names: "Harris"
    given-names: "Marcus"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MarcusHarrisUConn/mlmr"
url: "https://marcusharrisphd.com/mlmr/"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "R"
  - "Shiny"
  - "multilevel modeling"
  - "mixed-effects models"
  - "reproducible research"
abstract: >-
  mlmr is an open-source R package and Shiny application for fitting,
  understanding, and reporting mixed-effects and multilevel models. It provides
  an HLM-style graphical workflow while preserving transparent lme4 syntax,
  equations, diagnostics, APA-style tables, and reproducible exports.
